  "worked_solution": "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (8-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8t-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0)=-\\frac{5}{2}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{2} & =8(0)-\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{3}+C \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} & =0+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=8t-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{3}-\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=3\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =8(3)-\\frac{1}{2}(3)^{3}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =24-\\frac{27}{2}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =24-16 \\\\  & =8\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $8\\,\\text{m/s}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
